flowchart TD
  A["1. a new interactive zsh starts — the entire rc body is GENERATED by nix/zsh.nix initExtra, so never hand-edit ~/.zshrc"] --> B
  B["2. history hooks — __hist_pending_cmd plus precmd _hist_drop_failed, a command that exits non-zero is written and then dropped back out of HISTFILE"] --> C
  C["3. zinit sourced from the nix store, no runtime self-clone, but plugins zinit installs still land in the writable ~/.local/share/zinit because they are not part of the declarative config"] --> D
  D["4. oh-my-posh init zsh against the VENDORED theme zsh/oh-my-posh-catppuccin-mocha.omp.json, vendored rather than read from the store so it can carry a right-aligned execution-time segment and a transient prompt"] --> E
  E["5. export COLUMNS — zsh keeps it current but does not export it, and the theme path max_width template is evaluated by oh-my-posh which is a CHILD process that cannot see it otherwise"] --> F
  F["6. TRAPWINCH re-renders through _omp_get_prompt and zle reset-prompt, because oh-my-posh bakes PS1 into a literal string in precmd so a resize leaves the prompt and its dotted filler stale until the next command"] --> G
  G["7. zinit ice blockf then a compinit re-run — blockf stops the plugin fpath being added twice, and home-manager already ran compinit before this block"] --> H
  H["8. repo function files sourced — zsh/chrome-devtools-axi.zsh, agent-containers.zsh, little-coder.zsh, homebrew.zsh, table-view.zsh, fkill.zsh"] --> I
  I["9. LAST, ~/.zshrc.local when it exists — first adoption folds any pre-nix ~/.zshrc content in here so it keeps being sourced instead of only being backed up"]

  Theme["catppuccin mocha is shared across three files — this theme, @catppuccin_flavor in nix/tmux.nix, and the nvim colorscheme. Changing the flavor means changing all three"]
  D -.-> Theme
  A -.->|"every change here still needs ./setup.sh, see flows/apply-config.mmd"| Apply["nix/zsh.nix"]
